  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Towards Malaria Elimination: Expanding Test, Track, and Treat in Mining Areas - Suriname (01-Apr-2015-31-Mar-2018)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Suriname, Malaria, Ministry of Health, Welfare and Labour (MOH)This program has the following goals: Reduce the incidence of Malaria to less than 1 case per 1000 inhabitants in every region. The objectives of this program are: Achieve more than 90% coverage of LLIN&apos;s in selected high risk and vulnerable population.  Achieve parasitology confirmation of all cases.  Increase the percentage of Malaria knowledge.  Track and report 90% of the cases with diagnosis.  Treat freely 95% of malaria cases</narrative>
  </description>
